# Carry out this narrative request

Continue the supplied simulation story plausibly and in line with its purpose.
Write a finished continuation of {{target_min_words}}-{{target_max_words}} words, never more than {{number_of_words}}.
Use short sentences and spend the word budget on the requested events rather than commentary.

The current continuation requirements, repeated after the history, specify the transition to perform.
Fulfill ALL of them in this output. Recent interactions are the starting state, not permission to replace a requested ending or customer transition with another development of the old situation.

You are authorized to invent plausible new environmental events and supporting characters.
When the request explicitly delegates an action to the narrator (such as ending an engagement and beginning work on another), narrate that action at the level actually authorized.
Beginning work means scoping, requesting evidence or examining supplied information, not inventing an analysis or successful intervention.
Do not invent personal memories, preferences or choices for autonomous agents outside that delegation.

An ending must stop the active episode, not leave the same decision pending.
External consequences or a limited closeout can provide closure without solving every unknown.
A requested new engagement must actually introduce a different customer and problem and start the permitted work; do not remain with the old customer.
A normal open continuation should instead provide a concrete new situation the agents can respond to, without determining their choices.
Do not repeat a previous continuation.
