Keep the chronology and supplied facts; handle elapsed time realistically.
If evidence is still missing at closeout, retain that limitation rather than inventing findings.
A moral, when requested, must follow from what actually changes.
Return only the continuation, without headings or word counts.
Aim for {{target_min_words}}-{{target_max_words}} words so the {{number_of_words}}-word ceiling has a real safety margin.
